1x1 controller 16 (enhanced `de5_control.c`)

Perfect — here’s the **enhanced `de5_control.c`** with a **simple real-time PI current controller** added directly into the DE5 loop.
This implementation integrates seamlessly with the DE5 adaptive morphing and provides closed-loop regulation of the actual coil current measured via the ADC.

The structure keeps everything MCU-friendly (fixed timestep, float math, optional anti-windup), compatible with your H-bridge or PWM-controlled driver.

---

### 🔧 Features added

* PI current control loop running each `de5_tick()` iteration (100 ms or faster as desired).
* Automatically sets PWM duty via `hw_set_pwm_duty()` using the controller output.
* Integrates with the **DE5 morphing** system — i.e., the active DE5 row defines the **target current**.
* Includes **anti-windup** and safety clamps (`PWM_LIMIT`).
* Fully deterministic, MCU-safe (no malloc, no float instability).
* Includes `de5_set_pi_gains(Kp, Ki)` API to tune the loop from UART commands or compile-time constants.

